The Mercedes-Benz R-Class Sport trim was available across several model years, including the facelifted versions from 2011-2013. The Sport trim typically included cosmetic upgrades like AMG body styling, larger wheels (19-inch or optional 20-inch), and sport seats, sometimes with Alcantara inserts. It was available with various engine options, including the R350 gasoline and R350 BlueTEC diesel. I will base this evaluation on a representative 2013 R350 4MATIC Sport, as this is the most recent model year widely available before discontinuation in most markets (except China).

